comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:14:23.415Z",codex-agent,"Native real-tracker tests passed: every request/record boundary has an interleaved competing write; process interruption before and after guard/update/receipt converges under the original operation key. Two OS reservation writers admit exactly one reservation, rejecting the stale writer with zero history effect. Additional two-OS outcome and create-boundary checks are included for the final full gate. Privacy and byte capacity refuse before writes. The 500 seeded random operation sequences passed against independent journal state and SDK read-back."
  "2026-11-06T12:49:23.275Z",codex-agent,"The first isolated linked protocol group exceeded the native 120-second default on the shared host. Its failure record is retained. Set this newly linked command timeout to 600 seconds and rerun unchanged assertions with two workers; this does not alter any coverage, lint or release threshold."
  "2026-11-06T13:30:26.594Z",codex-agent,"All linked checks now pass: kernel 7, protocol 18, proof/workflow 9 and epic 11 tests on the recorded snapshots. The isolated protocol timeout was retained and the unchanged 18-test group passed with the command-specific 600-second allowance. Final focused checks after certificate and owner-identity strengthening pass 12 tests. Final packed rehearsal passes 45 CLI invocations per npm/Bun journey, SDK writes/replay, capacity and invalid-certificate/unsupported-host boundaries. Final full release checks will run on the committed candidate."
  "2026-11-06T16:50:55.064Z",codex-agent,"Validated and fixed creation identity admission with normalizeId or explicit native idPrefix, bounded fitter-independent refusals, native exit preservation, adapter JSON object-root validation, exact inert TOON round trips, home-path scope, and shared-graph traversal bounds. Regression tests use real native trackers; unsafe creation checks its own absent history file, and legacy privacy fixtures are persisted with consistent journal digests before read-back."
  "2026-11-06T18:14:52.257Z",codex-agent,Final inspection also preserved the receiver of a host-provided normalizeId method before applying it to owner and relationship identities. The real tracker test uses a method that asserts its native receiver; removing the binding fails its named regression. Creation still accepts the explicit idPrefix fallback and refuses an absent identity policy before effects.
